# npm install output. Never committed; `npm ci` reproduces it exactly from
# the committed package-lock.json.
node_modules/

# npm/vite scratch output.
npm-debug.log*
.vite/
*.local

# NOT ignored, deliberately, and both are easy to get wrong:
#
#   dist/     docs/web-frontend-spec.md says "web/dist is gitignored". That
#             is now obsolete: web/embed.go embeds it with `//go:embed
#             all:dist`, and a missing embed target is a hard *compile*
#             error, so an ignored (and therefore absent) dist/ breaks
#             `go build ./...` on any clean checkout without Node. dist/
#             instead ships committed placeholders, per the rationale in
#             web/embed.go. `npm run build` overwrites those placeholders
#             with real Vite output -- that shows up as a dirty tree, and
#             the build artefacts are not meant to be committed. Restore
#             with `git checkout -- dist && git clean -fd dist`.
#             loam-nvb.15 owns the build/embed wiring and the final call on
#             whether real output ever gets committed.
#
#   src/gen/  Generated TypeScript (protoc-gen-es + protoc-gen-connect-query,
#             landing in loam-nvb.2) is committed, mirroring the Go side:
#             internal/gen is committed and CI enforces zero drift by
#             re-running codegen and failing on a diff. Committing the TS
#             keeps `npm run build` and `npm test` working without a
#             codegen step, exactly as docs/web-frontend-spec.md -> Codegen
#             specifies, and lets the same drift check cover the web side
#             once `task web:generate` exists.
